<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Argentovaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">378</span> · Also known as Battle of Argentaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Argentovaria was fought in 378 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> between the Western Roman army of the emperor Gratian and the Alemannic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lentienses">Lentienses</a>, who had crossed the frozen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. Gratian's generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nannienus">Nannienus</a> and the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallobaudes">Mallobaudes</a> crushed the invaders and killed their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/priarius">Priarius</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> reports that only about 5,000 of them escaped. Gratian then crossed the Rhine and forced the Lentienses to submit.</p></div>
